# Variable Validation Workflow

After creating or updating any page/component UI (especially colors, borders, backgrounds, icons, and text styles), run the `/check-variables` command guidance in `.cursor/commands/check-variables.md`.

For changed TypeScript and TSX files, also run ESLint and resolve every
`shadcn/no-raw-colors` warning in those files. This automatic check catches raw
palette colors and undeclared color names. Keep the contextual review below:
the linter cannot decide whether a valid token has the correct intent or
strength for the design.

Expected output format:
- One line per issue
- If no issues: `All variables applied correctly.`

Validation source of truth:
- `docs/COLOR_INVENTORY.md`
- `.cursor/rules/v3-color-system-usage.mdc`
